Churro: VK_ANDROID_external_memory_android_hardware_buffer for NVK (missing upstream).

Chrome (and Google apps that are Chrome PWAs, e.g. Calendar) renders through its own ANGLE on
Vulkan; without AHB support ANGLE can't wrap AHardwareBuffers, Chrome's GPU process finds no
backing for its display buffers and restarts forever (blank tabs/pages). Uses the common
vk_android helpers like panvk: AHB images are created deferred and laid out from the buffer
(linear dma-buf, explicit modifier layout) when memory is bound; AHB memory imports the buffer's
dma-buf (the AHB keeps owning the fd).

